CHECKS += check-mp4resume
#| MP4 back after a power-off: the `mp4.resume` row written and read back (playing or paused, an
#| album's or Shuffle All's queue, the second, the file), a broken one refused; a session counted
#| second by second (a write when a queue starts, every 30 s of playing, at a pause, a new song or
#| a power-off, none while paused); then the real launcher started in desk mode's dummy window on
#| the README's media card with a song's, a book's, a video's and Shuffle All's row: Now Playing
#| paused at its second, the row then saying paused so the next start opens nothing; nothing for a
#| paused row, a broken one or one whose file is gone (which takes it away); and a start that goes
#| back into a game a power-off left running (a Diatom of the check's own on the resident's
#| socket), a video's or a song's row: the game first, at its state with its menu up, MP4 held
#| under it with nothing of its own drawn, and SELECT in that menu Now Playing on it, Paused. Every
#| wait in a start is for an event (the screen it starts on drawn, the screen each key opens drawn,
#| the row saying what it should), never a time or a count of frames, so a loaded runner is only
#| slower; a string drawn is found wherever its line begins (on Linux with no sound card ALSA's
#| complaints can come first on it); a wait that runs out prints the start's own lines
